---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { getCollection, render } from 'astro:content';

const entries = (await getCollection('gallery')).sort(
  (a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf()
);
const projects = [...new Set(entries.map((e) => e.data.project))].sort();
const rendered = await Promise.all(
  entries.map(async (entry) => ({ entry, Content: (await render(entry)).Content }))
);
---
<Base title="Gallery · Fourth Wall Gaming" description="AI-generated art, film, and comics from Fourth Wall Gaming worlds.">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Gallery</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      What the games left behind — the novels written out of played sessions, and the art generated
      alongside the worlds. Every piece is tied to the canon it illustrates.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-head">Novelizations</h2>
    <p class="section-note">
      Each of these was a played session before it was prose. The dice had already fallen; the book
      is written afterwards from the campaign's own journal and play transcript, so the plot is
      whatever the players actually did with it. Read them as records, not as fiction written to a
      plan.
    </p>
    <ul class="novels">

      <li class="card novel">
        <h3><a href="/novels/the-kestrel-of-lanternfall.pdf">The Kestrel of Lanternfall</a></h3>
        <p class="meta">The Veilwrack · Sefa Rocksquill · 38 pages · PDF, 9.6 MB</p>
        <p>The sky-realm on the bone-spires of dead leviathans, and the wind itself failing. Three
        chapters from the opening run — the ninth night, the last supper, the closed hand.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card novel">
        <h3><a href="/novels/and-then-the-dragons-came-purewater.pdf">And Then the Dragons Came: Purewater</a></h3>
        <p class="meta">Purewater · Magda · 72 pages · PDF, 0.3 MB</p>
        <p>A seventy-year-old pilgrim of Hel walks three hundred miles into a canal city on the eve
        of the Lake Lady's Tourney, carrying a quarterstaff and eleven nights of the same dream.</p>
        <p class="also">Also as <a href="/novels/and-then-the-dragons-came-purewater-authors-cut.pdf">the Author's Cut</a> — the same play at 174 pages (0.9 MB) in a different prose voice, which is the clearest look at what the style setting actually does.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card novel">
        <h3><a href="/novels/the-short-ledger.pdf">The Short Ledger</a></h3>
        <p class="meta">Purewater · Kag · 113 pages · PDF, 0.6 MB</p>
        <p>The same city from underneath: a collector working the water-stairs for the local crime
        lord, and a ledger that does not add up. Dialogue lifted from the play transcript rather
        than paraphrased from the journal.</p>
      </li>

      <li class="card novel">
        <h3><a href="/novels/the-wrong-cathedral.pdf">The Wrong Cathedral</a></h3>
        <p class="meta">GoblinPak · Vek and Vosh · 168 pages · PDF, 0.8 MB</p>
        <p>Gobtown, the first goblinoid city that works, held together by deals nobody has read all
        of. Two goblins, nine chapters, and a rent problem.</p>
      </li>

    </ul>

    <h2 class="section-head">Art</h2>

    {entries.length === 0 && (
      <div class="card empty-state">
        <p><em>The gallery is being hung. First pieces arriving soon.</em></p>
      </div>
    )}

    {entries.length > 0 && (
      <div class="filters" id="filters">
        <button data-project="all" class="active">All</button>
        {projects.map((p) => <button data-project={p}>{p}</button>)}
      </div>
    )}

    <div class="gallery-grid">
      {rendered.map(({ entry, Content }) => (
        <figure class="card gallery-item" data-project={entry.data.project}>
          <Image src={entry.data.image} alt={entry.data.title} width={800} />
          <figcaption>
            <h3>{entry.data.title}</h3>
            <p class="meta">{entry.data.project} · {entry.data.medium} · {entry.data.tools.join(', ')}</p>
            <Content />
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    .lede { color: var(--text-dim); max-width: 38rem; }
    .section-head { margin-top: 3rem; }
    .section-note { color: var(--text-dim); max-width: 42rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }
    .novels { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; display: grid; gap: 1.25rem;
              grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(20rem, 1fr)); }
    .novel { padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem; }
    .novel h3 { margin: 0 0 0.3rem; font-size: 1.15rem; }
    .novel .meta { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-dim); text-transform: uppercase;
                   letter-spacing: 0.05em; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
    .novel p { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-dim); margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
    .novel p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .novel .also { font-size: 0.875rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 0.6rem; }
    .empty-state { max-width: 28rem; margin: 2.5rem auto; text-align: center; }
    .filters { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
    .filters button {
      background: var(--bg-raised);
      color: var(--text-dim);
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 0.35rem 1rem;
      cursor: pointer;
      font: inherit;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
    .filters button.active { border-color: var(--amber); color: var(--amber); }
    .gallery-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: 1.25rem;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(18rem, 1fr));
    }
    .gallery-item { margin: 0; padding: 0; overflow: hidden; }
    .gallery-item :global(img) { width: 100%; }
    .gallery-item figcaption { padding: 1rem 1.25rem 1.25rem; }
    .gallery-item .meta { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-dim); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
    .gallery-item.hidden { display: none; }
  </style>

  <script>
    const buttons = document.querySelectorAll('#filters button');
    const items = document.querySelectorAll('.gallery-item');
    buttons.forEach((btn) => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        buttons.forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
        btn.classList.add('active');
        const project = (btn as HTMLElement).dataset.project;
        items.forEach((item) => {
          (item as HTMLElement).classList.toggle(
            'hidden',
            project !== 'all' && (item as HTMLElement).dataset.project !== project
          );
        });
      });
    });
  </script>
</Base>
